@* The one `<meta name="robots" content="noindex">`: the pages search engines have no business
   indexing — search results, not-found and error surfaces, admin and editor pages, and
   non-published posts — render this instead of writing the tag themselves. The element is bare
   on purpose: Blazor's HeadOutlet renders the content of exactly one HeadContent per page (a
   HeadContent registers as a section provider and the outlet keeps a single one), so each page
   puts this inside its own HeadContent — SeoHead does the same for draft and scheduled posts. *@
<meta name="robots" content="noindex" />
